# Classless themes

## Source of truth

- **`css.html`** — catalog of nested-tag contracts. Every new theme must style these demos and be checked by flipping the Theme control.
- **`css2.html`** — composed layout examples (full page structure). Use it to verify nesting still works when patterns are combined; keep it theme-switchable.
- Do **not** invent presentational classes. Prefer element selectors and nesting. Thin hooks OK: `data-theme`, `data-tone`, `data-backdrop`, `aria-label="Theme"`.

## Nesting contracts (must differ by parent)

| Selector | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `article` | Padded surface + vertical margin |
| `article > article` | Nested surface, **no** extra vertical margin |
| `article aside` | Text callout (accent edge) — **not** a card |
| `section aside` | Fixed-width **card** (links centered) |
| `article > fieldset` | Shaded inset |
| `article > section > header:first-child` | Title bar only on the **first** header |
| `section > header > fieldset` | Full-width blurb / badge |
| `section article` | Inverted / primary accent panel |
| `fieldset > details > figure` | Bordered, padded figure |
| `header nav` vs `nav` | Inverted bar vs surface bar; same dropdown behavior |
| `form nav` | Inline actions — not a site menu |
| `footer nav` | Space-between meta row (often two `ul`s) |

## Shared behavior across themes

- **Nav dropdowns**: hidden nested `ul`, show on `li:hover`, absolute position, `::before` hover bridge (match `nxpt.css` behavior; theme only colors/elevation).
- **`data-tone`**: `primary` \| `inverse` \| `accent` on cards/fieldsets — themes own colors (no inline style).
- **`body[data-backdrop="photo"]`**: optional photo chrome (home); solid body otherwise.
- **Links**: `a` text; `a b`/`a strong` filled buttons; `a i`/`a em` outline buttons.
- Register new themes in `js/theme-switch.js` and both Theme `<select>`s (`index.html`, `css.html`; keep `css2.html` in sync).

## When adding a theme

1. Add `css/<name>.css` covering **all** `css.html` fieldset demos (TOC names).
2. Wire the switcher; default remains `nxpt` until the new theme is ready.
3. A/B on `css.html`, then spot-check composition on `css2.html` and `index.html`.
4. If you discover a new nest worth documenting, **add it to `css.html` first** — then implement it in every theme.
